WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.166 --> 00:00:18.648
dropped down on a park bench.

2
00:00:18.668 --> 00:00:23.971
"I shouldn't have told Kate that I lost my phone," Ally thought.

3
00:00:24.392 --> 00:00:27.194
"That was a big lie—and a big mistake!"

4
00:00:28.054 --> 00:00:29.936
But Ally hadn't known what else to do.

5
00:00:31.432 --> 00:00:34.054
She couldn't let Kate find out the truth about Alpha.

6
00:00:34.494 --> 00:00:35.574
It was too dangerous.

7
00:00:35.594 --> 00:00:38.036
"I know," she thought.

8
00:00:38.056 --> 00:00:42.298
"I'll leave Alpha home until I blast off with Lainie.

9
00:00:42.658 --> 00:00:47.441
And then, when it's time to go, I'll pretend I found the phone— and give it to Kate

10
00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:49.002
as my going-away present!"

11
00:00:50.423 --> 00:00:53.424
Happy she'd come up with a good plan, Ally hurried home.

12
00:00:57.626 --> 00:01:00.168
She went to her room and turned Alpha back on.

13
00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:06.969
"Alpha, I have to tell you my great idea for a going-away gift for Mateo," she said.

14
00:01:06.989 --> 00:01:13.711
"I'm going to throw a party, so we can celebrate all of the Earthlings' Holly Days at once,

15
00:01:13.791 --> 00:01:14.672
before we leave.

16
00:01:15.632 --> 00:01:17.672
Except I don't know what they are.

17
00:01:18.293 --> 00:01:20.253
Can you look up Holly Days?

18
00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:24.454
They sound a bit like Astral Days on Astralia."

19
00:01:25.515 --> 00:01:30.556
"Affirmative." The old phone hummed and buzzed as Alpha worked to get the information.

20
00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:33.873
"I located a record for holly.

21
00:01:34.774 --> 00:01:37.515
It is a plant with spiky leaves and red berries.

22
00:01:38.036 --> 00:01:40.997
It is a traditional Christmas decoration," Alpha said.

23
00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:45.060
"Interesting. But what's Christmas?"

24
00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.901
Alpha buzzed again.

25
00:01:46.921 --> 00:01:52.924
"Christmas is a religious holiday celebrated mainly by Christian Earthlings in December.

26
00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:57.487
Hannukah is celebrated by Jewish Earthlings around the same time.

27
00:01:58.167 --> 00:02:04.187
And Kwanzaa is a celebration of life and African heritage, also celebrated in December."

28
00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:07.989
"Are there any other Holly Days I should know about?"

29
00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:09.010
Ally asked.

30
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.612
"In November some Earthlings celebrate Thanksgiving.

31
00:02:13.212 --> 00:02:18.955
Valentine's Day is celebrated in February, and Lunar New Year is in January or February.

32
00:02:19.315 --> 00:02:21.717
Passover and Easter are in the spring."

33
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:24.938
"Earthlings have so many Holly Days!"

34
00:02:25.379 --> 00:02:26.219
Ally exclaimed.

35
00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:30.890
"Alpha, please make a list of foods people eat on Holly Days."

36
00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:34.833
"Affirmative." A few minutes later, Alpha reported back.

37
00:02:34.853 --> 00:02:42.939
"People eat turkey and stuffing for Thanksgiving Alpha made a strange, loud, crackling noise.

38
00:02:43.619 --> 00:02:44.260
Ally looked up.

39
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.161
"Are you okay?"

40
00:02:46.181 --> 00:02:48.203
"I'm fine."

41
00:02:48.723 --> 00:02:51.405
Alpha went back to reporting the information about foods.

42
00:02:51.425 --> 00:02:55.148
"They give red chocolate hearts on Christmas.

43
00:02:56.072 --> 00:03:00.876
They paint eggs for Valentine's Day, and chocolate sauce is poured on the Thanksgiving turkey."

44
00:03:00.896 --> 00:03:05.079
"Everything sounds so fun!"

45
00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:05.959
Ally said.

46
00:03:05.979 --> 00:03:10.382
"This is going to be the perfect going-away present for Mateo.

47
00:03:11.303 --> 00:03:13.424
Can you please make a shopping list for me?"

48
00:03:13.444 --> 00:03:16.307
"Preparing it now," Alpha said.

49
00:03:16.327 --> 00:03:20.890
"Thanks. Now I just have to figure out when to have the party.

50
00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.812
It has to be before I leave with Lainie Polk."

51
00:03:24.864 --> 00:03:27.906
"T-minus two weeks to blastoff," Alpha said.

52
00:03:27.926 --> 00:03:30.708
"Whoa! That's soon!"

53
00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:33.370
Ally suddenly realized something.

54
00:03:33.911 --> 00:03:35.592
"I haven't heard from Lainie lately.

55
00:03:36.072 --> 00:03:37.674
Have I missed any calls from her?"

56
00:03:37.694 --> 00:03:42.717
"Negative. Last incoming communication was exactly 13 days ago."

57
00:03:42.737 --> 00:03:44.058
"That's odd.

58
00:03:44.418 --> 00:03:46.140
Let's call her," Ally said.

59
00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.664
Lainie's assistant answered the phone.

60
00:03:52.224 --> 00:03:54.626
"Sorry, Ally, but Lainie is out of the office."

61
00:03:55.166 --> 00:03:57.388
"Okay, can you ask her to call me back?"

62
00:03:57.809 --> 00:03:58.389
Ally asked.

63
00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.132
"I'm afraid she's out of the country without any cell service.

64
00:04:02.472 --> 00:04:04.074
I'll have her call you when she returns."

65
00:04:04.094 --> 00:04:05.154
"Thank you."

66
00:04:05.795 --> 00:04:06.375
Ally hung up.

67
00:04:06.395 --> 00:04:10.058
"Reply does not compute," Alpha said.

68
00:04:10.078 --> 00:04:11.860
"Sure, it does."

69
00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.522
Silly Alpha—she was acting up again.

70
00:04:14.542 --> 00:04:18.405
"Lainie will call me as soon as she's back.

71
00:04:19.045 --> 00:04:21.888
But, Alpha, I need you to stay quiet today.

72
00:04:22.464 --> 00:04:27.467
Don't make any noise at all, except for text messages and when Lainie calls.

73
00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.409
Understand?" "Hmpf!"

74
00:04:31.989 --> 00:04:33.250
Alpha made a snorting noise.

75
00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.191
"I understand loud and clear!"

76
00:04:35.551 --> 00:04:38.613
The screen turned black as Alpha went into Sleep mode.

77
00:04:40.594 --> 00:04:44.036
Later Ally walked back into town to meet Mateo at the print shop.

78
00:04:44.676 --> 00:04:47.558
She brought Alpha because she was still waiting for Lainie's call.

79
00:04:48.118 --> 00:04:51.100
As she walked along, she noticed flyers posted everywhere.

80
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.422
She stopped to read one: "Lost Phone!

81
00:04:55.842 --> 00:04:57.463
Reward for Its Safe Return."

82
00:04:57.483 --> 00:05:00.305
"That's sad," Ally thought.

83
00:05:00.325 --> 00:05:02.147
"Someone lost their phone."

84
00:05:02.707 --> 00:05:06.269
But then Ally looked closer and saw the photo on the flyers.

85
00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.752
It was a picture of Ally with Alpha in her hand.

86
00:05:09.772 --> 00:05:11.513
"Oh no!"

87
00:05:11.953 --> 00:05:13.735
Ally groaned.

88
00:05:13.755 --> 00:05:18.738
"Now people all over town will be looking for my phone—and me!

89
00:05:18.758 --> 00:05:21.020
I should have left Alpha at home!"

90
00:05:21.664 --> 00:05:24.167
Just then Alpha buzzed with a text message.

91
00:05:25.007 --> 00:05:29.852
It was from Kate: I'll have final T-shirt designs for you later today.

92
00:05:29.872 --> 00:05:35.517
"Alpha, write back and say, 'Thanks for Ally remembered something.

93
00:05:35.537 --> 00:05:37.399
"Wait! Never mind!

94
00:05:37.939 --> 00:05:41.142
I told Kate I lost my phone, so I can't reply.

95
00:05:41.763 --> 00:05:44.626
Instead I have to pretend I didn't see the text.

96
00:05:45.487 --> 00:05:46.708
Ugh!" Ally groaned.

97
00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:52.491
"Life is so much easier on Astralia, where we can read one another's minds!"
